# BuildKit reads this file (named "<dockerfile>.dockerignore") when the build
# uses -f apps/web/Dockerfile, taking precedence over any root .dockerignore.
# The build context is the REPOSITORY ROOT (see apps/web/Dockerfile), so these
# patterns are relative to the repo root.
#
# Keep out build artifacts, VCS, local env, and editor cruft. Do NOT exclude
# workspace source or manifests — the multi-stage build needs every workspace
# package.json (for the frozen-lockfile install) plus packages/core and
# apps/web source.
**/node_modules
**/.next
**/.turbo
**/dist
**/out
**/build
**/coverage
**/.git
**/.github
**/.vercel
**/.expo
**/*.tsbuildinfo
**/.DS_Store
**/npm-debug.log*
**/yarn-error.log*

# Never ship env files into the image (but keep the checked-in example).
**/.env
**/.env.*
!**/.env.example
